abstract: >-
  Replication package for a model-behaviour study of a Kandler-family
  demographic agent-based model, motivated by the case of Slavic
  linguistic expansion in the early-medieval Balkans (c. 600–860 CE)
  and calibrated against the documented Arabic expansion
  (c. 630–800 CE). The package contains the engine (frozen at
  commit 37054ac), all sweep scripts, the canonical per-cell run
  artefacts, the per-sweep durable record logs, and the
  paper-ready ODD-protocol model description, parameter
  justification table, results tables, four figures with
  generator scripts, and the reproducibility statement covering
  five inherited implementation defects identified and corrected
  during the systematic verification of the inherited
  published model.
